  "captureLimitations": [
    "Attempt-01 is preserved unchanged and invalid as a four-state mobile capture: its Input.synthesizeScrollGesture state branch left all four mobile states at y=0. Its captured-not-scored result is not a visual pass. Attempt-02 replaces only the formal evidence choice, using the existing exact mobile anchors and native end.",
    "Desktop source has a horizontal scrollbar: innerHeight=900, clientHeight=885, documentHeight=4617. The true native end is y=3732; using scrollHeight-innerHeight gives y=3717 and cannot represent the physical end. No source DOM, scrolling tolerance or production driver was changed.",
    "Source snapping moves 900px desktop / 844px phone per normal section. Fractions between snap points cannot substitute for actual reached states. Complete numbered-scene motion and the separate real finger forward/reverse path supply full-process evidence.",
    "The generic reduced pointer capture moves the pointer on the same final canvas but does not click swatches. Actual normal and reduced gray/blue/gray mouse and touch activation, stopped frames, and persistence through reverse/forward are in inputSupplement.",
    "Plain pointer movement did not visibly change the body; the actual signature control is color selection. Gray and blue actual product-body changes were directly viewed in the corresponding source screenshots.",
    "Actual Tab cycles did not reach the two source palette divs (tabIndex=-1, no role or accessible label). No keyboard palette success is claimed; purchase and external links were not activated.",
    "The phone true native endpoint y=4334 crops the top of the product in the final scene. The stable final section at y=4220 is separately retained in the scene-process evidence. This observed source limitation requires visual review and is not repaired in source capture."
  ],
